- op: discuss  # 7f65
  at: '2026-06-18T07:42:08Z'  # 7f65
  by: agent  # 7f65
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7f65
  clock: 3  # 7f65
  nonce: 7f65  # 7f65
  message: "SETTLED: BUG (not legitimate over-fire). Root cause in _python_context_fingerprint (fingerprint.py:222-265): for a DECORATED function whose producer-span starts at the def line (decorator excluded), the smallest covering node is the FunctionDef, but _py_effective_lines extends its start up to the decorator line (< span-start), so the 'covering node fits inside span' branch (line 249, lines[0] >= start_line) FAILS. Falls to the container-case (255), which walks only the FunctionDef children line-inside the span (body Return + return-annotation) and SKIPS the arguments node (no lineno) and never emits def:<name>. Net: hashes BODY ONLY, dropping name AND signature. Proof: analyze_rust(repo_root) vs analyze_js(repo_root,max_files=None) — diff signatures, same body -> same hgfp2:97672410; link_check(ctx) vs link_unmet(ctx) — diff names only -> same hgfp2:91e04b39. LATENT SCOPE: degrades fingerprint of EVERY decorated function whose span excludes the decorator (name+sig dropped); only VISIBLY collides on trivial-bodied stubs (these 44) because production bodies differ and mask it. FIX sketch: in the fit-check, accept a covering def/class as the match when its RAW node.lineno (post-decorator) >= start_line, so the whole def is walked (name+args captured). Churns fingerprint VALUES for decorated functions repo-wide (one-time; fingerprint is NOT a cache key, so no cache/run_signature hazard). Upgraded todo_soft->todo_hard (confirmed bug, broader than test stubs)."  # 7f65
