- op: discuss  # 9809
  at: '2026-06-18T08:48:03Z'  # 9809
  by: agent  # 9809
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9809
  clock: 5  # 9809
  nonce: '9809'  # 9809
  message: "INVESTIGATION COMPLETE (2-vantage workflow wf_160de918, behaviorally verified). Confirmed BUG; scope MUCH larger than the 44 visible stubs: a SINGLE AST-path root cause across ~1,043 decorated declaration nodes (768 function + 32 async + 243 class + @property) on the self-tree — every decorated def/class whose producer-span excludes the decorator. The 44 were just the VISIBLE collisions (trivial bodies); production decorated fns also have name+signature dropped, masked by differing bodies. TWO compounding drops in the container path (fingerprint.py:255-265): (1) def/class NAME (a node attribute emitted only when the node itself is walked at :190-193, skipped by the iter_child_nodes container walk); (2) arguments node (no lineno -> _py_effective_lines None -> skipped :259-260). Root: fit-check :249 (lines[0] >= start_line) uses the DECORATOR-EXTENDED start, so a decorated def whose span excludes the decorator fails the fit and degrades to a body-only hash. WI-falum (tree-sitter/TOML) is a SEPARATE already-fixed family, NOT a co-member (tree-sitter names are child nodes, immune). FIX (one edit, simulation-verified 0 residual on all 1,043): when best is FunctionDef/AsyncFunctionDef/ClassDef with best.lineno >= start_line and best.end_lineno <= end_line, route to the SUBTREE path (walk best whole) not the container path. Blast radius: 1,043 fingerprint VALUES change (3.1%), concentrated in decorated test files. fingerprint is NOT a cache key/run_signature input -> no cache hazard; one-time churn. REQUIRES TDD red/green on the real post-pass before closure (fix validated by isolated re-simulation, not a patched end-to-end build)."  # 9809
